  Cell[
   "Figure 2.1 of the book. f : X \[RightArrow] Y and g : U \[RightArrow] V."\
, "Text", FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], 
  Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], Cell["Bottom edge: two strands, X then U. \
Top edge: Y then V. So all three pictures are morphisms X \[CircleTimes] U \
\[RightArrow] Y \[CircleTimes] V.", "Item"], Cell["Left picture: f on the \
first strand and g on the second, at the same height: f \[CircleTimes] g.", 
   "Item"], Cell["Middle: f is lower (on X), g higher (on U): first f \
\[CircleTimes] id_U, then id_Y \[CircleTimes] g, so (id_Y \[CircleTimes] g)(f \
\[CircleTimes] id_U).", "Item"], Cell["Right: g first, then f: (f \
\[CircleTimes] id_V)(id_X \[CircleTimes] g). The text below the figure gives \
exactly these formulas.", "Item"], Cell["Transcription and checks", 
   "Subsection"], Cell["sig1 = \"f : X \[RightArrow] Y\\ng : U \[RightArrow] \
V\";\nfig21 = vee[#, sig1] & /@ {\"f \[CircleTimes] g\", \"(id_Y \
\[CircleTimes] g)(f \[CircleTimes] id_U)\", \"(f \[CircleTimes] id_V)(id_X \
\[CircleTimes] g)\"}", "Input"], 
