  Cell["(2.1): a pairing \[Omega] : X \[CircleTimes] Y \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 \
with inverse \[CapitalOmega] : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] Y \[CircleTimes] X.", 
   "Text", FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], 
  Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], Cell["Left picture, bottom: one strand Y at \
the right; \[CapitalOmega] (no inputs) at the bottom left. \[CapitalOmega] \
puts out two strands: Y (it goes up the left side to the top) and X (it goes \
up into \[Omega]).", "Item"], Cell["\[Omega] takes X (from \[CapitalOmega]) \
and Y (the source strand), and puts out nothing. Top edge: Y. So it is the \
morphism Y \[RightArrow] Y given by (id_Y \[CircleTimes] \
\[Omega])(\[CapitalOmega] \[CircleTimes] id_Y), and the picture says it \
equals id_Y.", "Item"], Cell["Layer by layer: \[CapitalOmega] at a = 0 on no \
strands; then \[Omega] at a = 1 on the strands X, Y. The right picture is the \
mirror image: (\[Omega] \[CircleTimes] id_X)(id_X \[CircleTimes] \
\[CapitalOmega]) = id_X.", "Item"], Cell["Transcription and checks", 
   "Subsection"], Cell["zz = {LD[{\"Y\"}, {{0, B[\"\[CapitalOmega]\", {}, \
{\"Y\", \"X\"}]}, {1, B[\"\[Omega]\", {\"X\", \"Y\"}, {}]}}], LD[{\"X\"}, \
{{1, B[\"\[CapitalOmega]\", {}, {\"Y\", \"X\"}]}, {0, B[\"\[Omega]\", {\"X\", \
\"Y\"}, {}]}}]};\n{validQ /@ zz, ldToExpression /@ zz}", "Input"], 
