  Cell["Figure 2.2. Arrows now carry the duals: an arc pointing down is X, an \
arc pointing up is X*.", "Text", FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], 
  Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], Cell["The key on the same page: ev_X and \
\:1ebdv_X are caps, coev_X and c\:0303oev_X are cups; which is which is read \
from the arrow on the arc.", "Item"], Cell["First picture: the source is the \
strand at the bottom right, pointing down, so X. It goes up into a cap on the \
right; the cap comes down into a cup on the left, which goes up to the top \
left. Bottom to top: the cup coev_X : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X \[CircleTimes] \
X* to the left of X, then the cap ev_X : X* \[CircleTimes] X \[RightArrow] \
\|01d7d9 on strands 2, 3. So (id_X \[CircleTimes] ev_X)(coev_X \[CircleTimes] \
id_X) = id_X.", "Item"], Cell["Third picture: the mirror image, with \:1ebdv \
and c\:0303oev: (\:1ebdv_X \[CircleTimes] id_X)(id_X \[CircleTimes] \
c\:0303oev_X) = id_X. The right half is the same with the arrows reversed, \
