  Cell["Figure 2.3: two expressions for f* : Y* \[RightArrow] X*.", "Text", 
   FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["Left picture: the source strand at the bottom left points up and is \
labelled Y, so it is Y*. To its right a cup (no inputs) puts out X (pointing \
down, into f) and X* (pointing up, to the top right): coev_X.", "Item"], 
  Cell["f turns X into Y, and a cap closes Y* (the source) with Y: ev_Y. The \
strand left at the top is X*, pointing up. So f* = (ev_Y \[CircleTimes] \
id_X*)(id_Y* \[CircleTimes] f \[CircleTimes] id_X*)(id_Y* \[CircleTimes] \
coev_X).", "Item"], 
  Cell["Right picture: the mirror image, with \:1ebdv_Y and c\:0303oev_X.", 
   "Item"], Cell["Transcription and checks", "Subsection"], 
