   "Output", CellTags -> "theta-left-twist", CellLabel -> "Book"], 
  Cell["The left twist \[Theta]\:02e1_X, drawn as a curl, with its formula.", 
   "Text", FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], 
  Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], Cell["A curl is read like any other diagram \
once it is cut into pieces: at the bottom a cup on the left (c\:0303oev_X, \
putting out X* and X), then a crossing of the two X strands (\[Tau]_{X,X}, \
the strand going up to the right passes over), then a cap on the left (ev_X \
on X* and X).", "Item"], Cell["Here the book also prints the formula, so the \
reading can be checked letter for letter: (ev_X \[CircleTimes] id_X)(id_X* \
\[CircleTimes] \[Tau]_{X,X})(c\:0303oev_X \[CircleTimes] id_X).", "Item"], 
  Cell["A crossing is the easiest thing to misread: over or under decides \
between \[Tau]_{X,X} (giving \[Theta]\:02e1) and \[Tau]\:207b\271_{X,X} \
(giving the inverse of \[Theta]\:02b3).", "Item"], 
  Cell["Transcription and checks", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["curl = textToLD[\"(ev_X \[CircleTimes] id_X)(id_{X*} \[CircleTimes] \
\[Tau]_{X,X})(coev~_X \[CircleTimes] id_X)\", \"X\"]", "Input"], 
