   "Output", CellTags -> "eq4-9-partition", CellLabel -> "Book"], 
  Cell["(4.9): for a 1-partition (p_\[Beta], q_\[Beta]) of X, with f : \
\|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X and g : X \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9.", "Text", 
   FontSlant -> Italic, FontSize -> 11], Cell["Reading", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["The red shapes are the book's notation for a partition \
(\[Section]4.6.1): the semi-disk is p_\[Alpha] : X \[RightArrow] i, the \
rectangle with a half-disk cut out is q_\[Alpha] : i \[RightArrow] X. Here \
they are not boxes with names written in them, so the text decides which is \
which.", "Item"], Cell["(4.7), bottom to top: i, then the rectangle \
q_\[Alpha] (i \[RightArrow] X), then the semi-disk p_\[Alpha] (X \
\[RightArrow] i), then i. So p_\[Alpha] q_\[Alpha], and the picture says it \
is N^i_X id_i, the multiplicity of i in X.", "Item"], 
  Cell["(4.9), left: f : \|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X at the bottom, then \
p_\[Beta] : X \[RightArrow] \|01d7d9 (the semi-disk, with nothing above it \
since the target is \|01d7d9 and \|01d7d9 is not drawn), then q_\[Beta] : \
\|01d7d9 \[RightArrow] X. So q_\[Beta] p_\[Beta] f = f. The right equation is \
the same upside down: g q_\[Beta] p_\[Beta] = g.", "Item"], 
  Cell["In Chapter 4 a diagram is a term of a linear combination: a \
coefficient, sums, the partition pairs, and the layered form. The pairs say \
which boxes are p_\[Alpha] and q_\[Alpha]: \"W\" is the object partitioned \
and \"t\" the simple object.", "Item"], Cell["Transcription and checks", 
   "Subsection"], Cell["term47 = <|\"c\" -> <|\"n\" -> 1, \"d\" -> 1, \"at\" \
-> <||>|>, \"sums\" -> {}, \"pairs\" -> <|\"\[Alpha]\" -> <|\"W\" -> {\"X\"}, \
\"t\" -> \"i\"|>|>,\n   \"ld\" -> LD[{\"i\"}, {{0, B[\"q_\[Alpha]\", {\"i\"}, \
{\"X\"}]}, {0, B[\"p_\[Alpha]\", {\"X\"}, \
{\"i\"}]}}]|>;\nsimplifyTermTrace[term47, \"Simples\" -> {\"i\"}] // Column", 
   "Input"], 
