  Cell["10. When a reading is wrong", "Section"], 
  Cell["Two typical errors, and what catches them.", "Text"], 
  Cell["10.1 A cap read as a cup", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["Read the first picture of Figure 2.2 top-down by mistake, and you get \
(id_X \[CircleTimes] coev_X)(ev_X \[CircleTimes] id_X). It is a valid \
diagram, but not a morphism X \[RightArrow] X: its source is X* \
\[CircleTimes] X \[CircleTimes] X. The type alone shows the reading is \
wrong:", "Text"], Cell["wrong = textToLD[\"(id_X \[CircleTimes] coev_X)(ev_X \
\[CircleTimes] id_X)\", \"X\"]; {First[wrong], typeOf[parseExpression[\"(id_X \
\[CircleTimes] coev_X)(ev_X \[CircleTimes] id_X)\"], parseSignature[\"X\"]]}"\
, "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
     {"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"X*\"", ",", "\"X\"", ",", 
            "\"X\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[
         {"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"X*\"", ",", "\"X\"", ",", 
                "\"X\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"X\"", ",", 
                "\"X\"", ",", "\"X*\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], 
   "Output"], Cell["10.2 A box on the wrong strand", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["Put f on the \[Or]X strand instead of the X strand in the definition \
of \[Or]f, and the type checker stops at once:", "Text"], 
  Cell["vee[\"(ev_Y \[CircleTimes] id_{\[Or]X})(id_{\[Or]Y} \[CircleTimes] \
id_X \[CircleTimes] f)(id_{\[Or]Y} \[CircleTimes] coev_X)\", \"f : X \
\[RightArrow] Y\"]", "Input"], Cell["expressionToLD::type: The composite \
\"id_\[Or]Y \[CircleTimes] id_X \[CircleTimes] f\" \[SmallCircle] \"id_\[Or]Y \
\[CircleTimes] coev_X\" does not fit: the target of the right factor is \
{\"\[Or]Y\", \"X\", \"\[Or]X\"}, but the left factor starts from {\"\[Or]Y\", \
\"X\", \"X\"}.", "Message", "MSG"], Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "Output"], 
  Cell["10.3 When the reading is right but the equation fails", 
   "Subsection"], Cell["Sometimes everything above passes and the book's \
equation still fails in the matrix model. That happened with Lemma 4.6(b) \
(notebook 10, graphical-calculus-4.nb): the figure was read correctly, the \
left side computes \[CapitalDelta]\:207a rather than dim(C), and with \
\[CapitalDelta]\:207a the equation holds. A check that fails after a correct \
reading points at the printed statement, not at the transcription.", "Text"], 
  Cell["11. Checks", "Section"], 
